    "lawCode": "Add §8-108, El L",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6216\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the election law, in relation to requiring the posting\nof information concerning a change in the location of a polling place\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nWhen there is a change of location of a polling place from the last\nprimary or general election held or when the last early voting period is\nheld, the Board of Elections shall be required to post at the entrance\nof the old polling location a notice on yellow paper informing voters\nthat the polling place has been moved and the street address of the new\nlocation.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 requires the Board of Elections, when there is a change of\nlocation of a polling place from the last primary or general election\nheld or the last early voting period is held, to post at the entrance of\nthe old polling location a notice on yellow paper informing voters that\nthe polling place has been moved and the street address of the new\nlocation. The notice must be posted on the day of the election or on the\nfirst day of early voting before the opening of the polls.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date which is immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nWhen polling places change, especially when they have been at one\nlocation for many years, voters are often confused and find out about\nthe change on the day of voting despite having been mailed a notice of\nthe change by the Board of Elections. A simple solution is to post a\nnotice of the change at the old polling site.\n\nWhen a polling place was moved for this past Election Day at a polling\nsite in the City of Newburgh, there was only a notice at the old\nlocation that it was no longer a polling site and the address of the new\nlocation was not stated. A campaign, upon noticing this omission, posted\na sign stating that the polling place had moved and the address of the\nnew location. This is not the proper way to post notice of a change of\nlocation of a polling site. The Board of Election should have the\nresponsibility to give proper notice on the day of voting at the old\nsite that the polling place has been moved and the location of the new\npolling place. This bill requires this action on the part of the Board\nof Elections.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019-20: A11164 - Referred to Election Law\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nMinimal.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
